@startuml agentic-value-stream-conformance-status-machine
' Per CR-VAS-004 §13 (Conformance Status) + §30 (Decision Rules).
' Cardinal author rule: Emmanuel A. Otchere <emmanuel@otchere.com>
' Last revised: 2026-10-08.

title Agentic Value Stream ; Conformance Status Machine

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false

state "Claimed" as CL
state "Under Review" as UR
state "Conditionally Conformant" as CC
state "Conformant" as CF
state "Non-Conformant" as NC
state "Expired" as EX

[*] -> CL : Instance Owner submits claim

CL -> UR : Semantic Validator begins assessment
UR -> CF : all mandatory AVS conditions PASS, materiality PASS, no exclusion
UR -> CC : mandatory evidence incomplete but no failure
UR -> NC : any mandatory condition fails OR exclusion triggered
UR -> NC : triggered exclusion overrides superficial positive evidence

CC -> CF : remaining evidence supplied and validated
CC -> NC : remaining gaps become failures
CC -> UR : re-validation requested

CF -> EX : evidence superseded by drift trigger
CF -> UR : re-validation requested
CF -> NC : drift detected, mandatory condition fails
CF -> NC : triggered exclusion

EX -> UR : re-submission begins re-validation

NC -> UR : re-submission begins re-validation

UR -> [*] : cancelled

note right of CF
  Conformant is a SEMANTIC state.
  It is independent of maturity
  (per CR-VAS-004 §14).

  A poorly performing AVS can
  remain semantically conformant.
end note

note right of NC
  Non-Conformant is determined
  by qualification evidence,
  not by telemetry volume or
  performance metrics.

  Telemetry is evidence, not
  semantics (per CR-VAS-004 §32).
end note

@enduml
